          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: запасной",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "запасной (zapasnóy) — \"spare, reserve\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "У меня есть запасной ключ. U menyá yest zapasnóy klyuch. I have a spare key."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Запасной выход — an emergency exit. Запасной план — a fallback plan."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "запасной (zapasnóy) is built on запас \"a store, a supply\", which is usually traced to пасти \"to guard, to keep\": what is kept in reserve."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
