              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "колебаться (kolebátsya) — \"to hesitate, to waver\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Я долго колебался, но потом согласился. Ya dólgo kolebálsya, no potóm soglasílsya. I hesitated for a long time, but then I agreed."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperfective; present колеблюсь, колеблешься. Literally to sway: пламя колеблется."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "колебаться (kolebátsya) is inherited from Proto-Slavic kolěbati (EtymDB), usually glossed \"to rock, to sway\"; a person who hesitates sways from one side to the other."
            }
          ]
        },
